---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Base
  lang={lang}
  title="Privacy Policy (App) | Breezer"
  description="Privacy policy for the Breezer app: what data is collected, how it is used, and your rights under the GDPR."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  noindex
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main class="pt-[120px] pb-16">
    <div class="dark:text-white">
          <div class="container mx-auto p-6 pt-[100px] bg-white dark:bg-stroke-dark rounded-lg shadow-md">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6">Privacy Policy App for Breezer</h1>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8"><strong>Last updated: 14.08.2026</strong></p>

            <p class="mb-4">At Breezer ("we", "our", or "us"), we value your privacy and are committed to protecting the personal
                information you share with us. This Privacy Policy App explains how we collect, use, store, and protect your
                data when you use the Breezer mobile application (the "App") and associated services (collectively, the
                "Service"). By using the App, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy App.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Controller</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">The controller responsible for the processing of your personal data within the meaning of Article 4(7)
                GDPR is:</p>
            <p class="mb-4">Klaus Siebeneicher<br />
                Am Sonnenhang 2<br />
                3243 St. Leonhard am Forst<br />
                Austria<br />
                <a href="mailto:info@breezer.now" class="text-blue-500 underline">info@breezer.now</a></p>
            <p class="mb-4">Full legal details are available in our <a href="/imprint" class="text-blue-500 underline">Imprint</a>.
                We have not appointed a data protection officer, as we are not required to do so.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">1. Introduction</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">Breezer is an app designed to help users track their snus consumption, set personalized limits, and analyze
                their consumption habits over time. We understand the importance of your privacy, and this Privacy Policy App
                explains how we handle your personal information. We want to ensure complete transparency about what data we
                collect, why we collect it, and how we protect it.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">2. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We collect and process the following types of data to provide and improve our Service:</p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.1 Personal Information</h3>
            <p class="mb-2">When you register and use the App, we collect the following personal data:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Email, username, and password:</strong> Used for account creation and authentication.</li>
                <li><strong>Profile picture (optional):</strong> You may choose to upload a profile picture for
                    personalization within the app.</li>
                <li><strong>Country and currency (optional):</strong> If provided in Settings, used to localize your
                    experience (e.g., pricing and statistics) and enable country-specific features such as regional
                    channels. Country may be considered personal data because it can relate to your location.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.2 Consumption and Quitting Data</h3>
            <p class="mb-2">We collect data related to your snus consumption and quitting progress, including:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Snus type, pack size, price per pack, and consumption limits:</strong> You can track your
                    consumption by entering the type of snus, its pack size, and price.</li>
                <li><strong>Consumption events:</strong> Records each time you log your consumption.</li>
                <li><strong>Quitting mode data:</strong> The date you started quitting, progress toward goals, and derived
                    achievement metrics such as money saved, time saved, and snus avoided.</li>
                <li><strong>Weekly, monthly, and yearly summaries:</strong> Insights into your usage, spending, and habits.</li>
                <li><strong>Health improvements display:</strong> Informational milestones based on studies. These are
                    estimates for motivation only and may be inaccurate. They are not medical advice.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">This information is processed only to deliver the app's functionality and to provide insights and
                motivation, and is used solely for tracking and analytical purposes.</p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.3 Usage Data</h3>
            <p class="mb-2">We automatically collect certain technical data when you use the app, including:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Device information:</strong> Such as device type, model, manufacturer, app version, operating
                    system version and language.</li>
                <li><strong>IP Address:</strong> For maintaining the security of our app.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.4 Product Analytics</h3>
            <p class="mb-2">To understand how the app is used and where it can be improved, we record a limited set of usage
                events:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li>Which screens you open, and when you use the app.</li>
                <li>Sign-up, login and your progress through onboarding.</li>
                <li>Whether the Breezer Pro offer was shown to you and what you did with it.</li>
                <li>Whether you are tracking or quitting, and when that changes.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">Where you tell us how much you use during onboarding, we record only a <strong>range</strong> (for
                example "11-20"), never the exact figure.</p>
            <p class="mb-4">These events are linked to an internal account identifier and your country. They are
                <strong>not</strong> linked to your email address or your username, and they <strong>never</strong> include
                your individual consumption entries, your chat messages or your uploaded images. See Section 7 for how to
                switch this off.</p>
            <p class="mb-4">As with any internet request, our analytics provider receives your device's IP address in order to
                receive the data at all. We have switched off the provider's location lookup, so your IP address is not used
                to derive your city or region.</p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.5 Crash and Error Reports</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">When the app crashes or hits an error, we receive a diagnostic report: the technical error, your
                device and app version, and a trail of what the app was doing beforehand. We do not attach your account
                identifier, email address or IP address to these reports, and they do not contain your consumption entries
                or chat messages.</p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.6 Community and Social Data</h3>
            <p class="mb-2">To provide global and country channels, mentions, and social features, we process:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Chat content and metadata:</strong> Messages you send, mentions, timestamps, and channel
                    membership. Channel messages are visible to participants and may be public to all users depending on
                    channel type.</li>
                <li><strong>Friends and notifications preferences:</strong> Which friends may receive updates about your
                    activity when enabled, and your opt-in/opt-out status for notifications.</li>
                <li><strong>Push notification tokens:</strong> Device tokens used to deliver notifications via Expo Push
                    Notifications API.</li>
                <li><strong>Moderation signals:</strong> Reports, blocks, and enforcement actions to keep the community safe.</li>
                <li><strong>Image files:</strong> Images uploaded to community chat (stored via Appwrite Cloud Storage).</li>
                <li><strong>Emoji reaction data:</strong> Which emoji you reacted to and on which message.</li>
                <li><strong>Automated activity announcements:</strong> System messages posted on your behalf when you reach certain milestones or change your quitting mode. These appear in community chat and include your username and avatar.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">2.7 Third-Party Content</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">The app includes a community feed that displays publicly available posts from Reddit via the Reddit API. Breezer does not store Reddit content permanently; it is fetched and cached temporarily for display purposes. No Reddit account or credentials are required. Reddit's own privacy policy governs content on their platform.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">3. Purpose of Data Collection</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We use your personal information for the following purposes:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">

                <li><strong>Account creation and authentication:</strong> Your email, username, and password help create and
                    secure your account.</li>
                <li><strong>Personalization and localization:</strong> The profile picture helps personalize your experience. Country and currency (if provided) help localize prices,
                    statistics, and enable regional features.</li>
                <li><strong>Statistics, insights, and motivation:</strong> Consumption and quitting data provide insights,
                    achievements, and motivational milestones.</li>
                <li><strong>Community features:</strong> To operate chats, country channels, mentions, and social visibility,
                    and to keep the community safe through moderation.</li>
                <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> To send opt-in updates to you and (if enabled) to your friends using Expo
                    Push Notifications.</li>
                <li><strong>Product analytics:</strong> To understand how the app is used, which features people reach, and
                    where they get stuck, so we can improve it.</li>
                <li><strong>Stability and security:</strong> To detect, diagnose and fix crashes and errors, and to protect
                    the app against abuse.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">We <strong>do not</strong> use your data for personalized marketing, ads, or sharing with third parties for
                advertising purposes.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">4. Sharing of Data with Third Parties</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We may share your data with the following third parties to help provide and improve our Service:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Appwrite Cloud (for data storage and management):</strong> We use Appwrite Cloud to store and manage
                    user data. Appwrite ensures secure data handling practices and complies with relevant data protection
                    standards.</li>
                <li><strong>RevenueCat (for subscription management):</strong> RevenueCat manages your Breezer Pro
                    subscription status. Your actual payment is processed by Apple or Google, depending on your platform;
                    we never see or store your payment card details.</li>
                <li><strong>Expo Push Notifications (for notifications delivery):</strong> Used to send push notifications to
                    your devices. Only device tokens and necessary metadata are shared for delivery.</li>
                <li><strong>Appwrite Cloud Storage (for image storage):</strong> Images uploaded in community chat are stored via Appwrite Cloud Storage.</li>
                <li><strong>PostHog (for product analytics):</strong> Receives the usage events described in Section 2.4.
                    Processed on PostHog's European Union infrastructure.</li>
                <li><strong>Sentry (for crash and error reporting):</strong> Receives the diagnostic reports described in
                    Section 2.5. Processed on Sentry's European Union infrastructure.</li>
                <li><strong>Reddit (for the community feed):</strong> The app requests publicly available posts from the
                    Reddit API for display. See Section 2.7.</li>
                <li><strong>ui-avatars.com (for fallback profile images):</strong> If you have not uploaded a profile picture,
                    the app generates a placeholder avatar from your initials. Your username is included in that image
                    request.</li>
                <li><strong>Expo (for app updates):</strong> The app checks Expo's update service for new versions, which
                    involves your device's IP address and an installation identifier.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">We ensure that all third parties we work with take appropriate security measures to protect your data.
                We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data, and we do not share it with data brokers or advertising
                networks.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">5. User Rights and Data Control</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">You have the following rights and control over your personal data:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Profile management:</strong> You can update your profile picture, country, currency, and
                    consumption/quitting data directly through the app.</li>
                <li><strong>Friends controls:</strong> You can choose to add/remove friends and to share consumption details like when a snus has been taken whith them.</li>
                <li><strong>Notifications control:</strong> You can opt in or out of push notifications anytime in Settings or
                    via your device settings.</li>
                <li><strong>Analytics control:</strong> You can stop sharing usage data at any time under <strong>Settings
                    -&gt; Policies -&gt; Share usage data</strong>. Switching it off stops all product analytics collection
                    from your device immediately, and does not affect any other part of the app.</li>
                <li><strong>Data deletion:</strong> If you wish to delete your account and associated data, you can do so by
                    sending an email to <a href="mailto:info@breezer.now" class="text-blue-500 underline">info@breezer.now</a> or by going to <strong>Settings
                    -> Account Settings -> Delete Account</strong> in the app.</li>
                <li><strong>Data access:</strong> You can request a summary of the data we hold about you. Please contact us at
                    <a href="mailto:info@breezer.now" class="text-blue-500 underline">info@breezer.now</a> to submit such a request.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">6. Data Security</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We take the security of your data seriously. To protect your personal information, we use the following security
                practices:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Encryption:</strong> Your data is stored securely using encryption provided by Appwrite Cloud.</li>
                <li><strong>Access control:</strong> Only authorized personnel have access to your data.</li>
                <li><strong>Regional storage:</strong> We aim to store data within the region where Appwrite Cloud operates for
                    your workspace. Push notification delivery is handled by Expo, which may process data across regions solely
                    to deliver notifications.</li>
                <li><strong>Analytics and crash data:</strong> Product analytics are processed by PostHog on their European
                    Union infrastructure, and crash reports by Sentry on their European Union infrastructure. Neither is
                    transferred outside the EU by us.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">While we take all reasonable precautions to protect your data, please note that no method of transmission over
                the Internet or method of electronic storage is 100% secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security, but we strive
                to implement robust security measures.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">7. Analytics and Tracking Technologies</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">The Breezer app does <strong>not</strong> use cookies or advertising identifiers, we do <strong>not</strong>
                track you across other apps or websites, and we do <strong>not</strong> track your activity for marketing or
                advertising purposes. There are no ads in the app.</p>
            <p class="mb-4">We do use two services to keep the app working and to improve it:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>PostHog</strong> for product analytics, so we can see how the app is used. The events it records
                    are described in Section 2.4. Screen recording is switched off, and we do not automatically capture
                    what you type or tap.</li>
                <li><strong>Sentry</strong> for crash and error reporting, so we can find and fix things that break. What it
                    receives is described in Section 2.5.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">You can turn product analytics off at any time under <strong>Settings -&gt; Policies -&gt; Share usage
                data</strong>. Switching it off stops all analytics collection from your device and does not affect any other
                part of the app. Crash reporting is not covered by this toggle, because we need it to keep the app usable for
                everyone.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">8. Policy Changes and Notification</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We may update this Privacy Policy App from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. If we
                make significant changes to how we handle your data, we will notify you through the app, by email, or through app
                store updates. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy App periodically for any updates.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">9. Legal Bases for Processing</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">Where the GDPR applies, we rely on the following legal bases:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR):</strong> Creating and securing your account, storing
                    and displaying your consumption and quitting data, operating community features, and managing your
                    Breezer Pro subscription. Without this processing the app cannot do what you installed it for.</li>
                <li><strong>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR):</strong> Push notifications, and sharing your activity with friends.
                    You can withdraw either at any time in Settings, with effect for the future.</li>
                <li><strong>Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR):</strong> Product analytics, crash and error reporting,
                    and security logging. Our legitimate interest is understanding and improving the app, keeping it stable,
                    and protecting it against abuse. You may object to product analytics at any time by switching off
                    <strong>Share usage data</strong> in Settings, which stops that processing immediately.</li>
                <li><strong>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR):</strong> Where we are required to retain or disclose data,
                    for example in response to a lawful request.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">10. Your Rights Under Data Protection Laws</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA) or another jurisdiction with data protection laws, you
                have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Right to access:</strong> You have the right to access the data we hold about you.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to rectification:</strong> You can request to correct any inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to erasure:</strong> You may request that we delete your data under certain conditions.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to restriction:</strong> You may ask us to limit the use of your data.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to portability:</strong> You can request a copy of your data in a structured, machine-readable
                    format.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to withdraw consent:</strong> If you provided consent for the processing of your data, you can
                    withdraw it at any time.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR):</strong> You may object to processing based on our legitimate
                    interests, including product analytics.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to lodge a complaint (Art. 77 GDPR):</strong> You may complain to a supervisory authority.
                    Ours is the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Österreichische Datenschutzbehörde, Barichgasse 40-42,
                    1030 Vienna, <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" class="text-blue-500 underline" rel="noopener">dsb.gv.at</a>),
                    but you may also complain to the authority where you live or work.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-4">For more details or to exercise any of these rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@breezer.now" class="text-blue-500 underline">info@breezer.now</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">11. Marketing and Promotional Communications</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">At present, Breezer does not engage in sending promotional communications, but this may change in the future. If we
                do send you marketing emails, you will have the option to opt-out by clicking the "unsubscribe" link in the email
                or updating your preferences in the app settings. Push notifications are sent only with your consent and can be
                disabled at any time in Settings or via your device settings.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">12. Data Retention</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">We will retain your personal data for as long as your account remains active. If you delete your account, we will
                delete all associated data as per our retention policy. Certain minimal logs (e.g., security and moderation
                logs) may be retained for a limited period as required for safety, fraud prevention, and legal compliance.
                Product analytics events and crash reports are retained only for the retention period configured in the
                respective service and are then deleted automatically. Because analytics events are not linked to your email
                address, deleting your account does not require us to delete them individually; you can stop new events being
                collected at any time using the toggle described in Section 7.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">13. Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">Breezer is not intended for use by anyone under the age of 18, in line with our
                <a href="/eula" class="text-blue-500 underline">End-User License Agreement</a>. If you are under 18, please do
                not use the app. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If we become aware that we have collected
                personal data from someone under 18, we will take steps to delete that data. Community features are moderated
                but may expose users to content shared by others; parental guidance is advised.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">14. Contact Information</h2>
            <p class="mb-4">If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy App, please contact us at:</p>
            <p class="mb-4"><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@breezer.now" class="text-blue-500 underline">info@breezer.now</a></p>
            <p class="mb-4"><strong>App Store Support:</strong> You can also reach us through the support options available in the app stores.</p>

            <div class="text-center mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
                <p>&copy; 2026 Breezer. All Rights Reserved.</p>
            </div></div>
        </div>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Base>
